    "title": "10 Regional Rivalries Americans Pretend Don't Exist (But Absolutely Do) - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Claudia Edwards ,\n6 hours ago America loves to play nice—but let’s be honest, the rivalries run deep. From coast to coast, cities, states, and entire regions quietly (or not so quietly) size each other up. It’s the South vs. the Midwest over barbecue. The East Coast scoffing at West Coast “winters.” Texans insisting everything’s bigger—while Californians roll their eyes. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
